```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason: `1result.sql` correctly  
• keeps only the first CPC code per patent,  
• reduces it to the level‑5 CPC symbol and filters with `cd.level = 5`,  
• calculates the EMA with the standard formula EMAₜ = 0.2·xₜ + 0.8·EMAₜ₋₁ (recursive CTE), starting from the first year’s actual count,  
• then selects, for every CPC group, the year whose EMA is maximal, and finally reports the required three columns.  
`2result.sql` starts its EMA with 0.2·x₁ (not x₁) and uses an imprecise non‑recursive window expression later, so its EMA values are biased downward and can be inconsistent; therefore `1result.sql` is the correct choice.